# Operator Command Lessons Learned

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Applies when **operator discovery** commands fail, return empty/wrong output, or the same broken paste pattern appears in multiple plans.

## Law (non-negotiable)

When an operator reports that a **Pending commands** block failed (wrong path, wrong user, missing overlay file, grep too broad, empty result, permission denied, etc.):

1. **Fix the plan in the same turn** — update **Operator discovery** on disk (`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`); record what failed in **Completed findings**.
2. **Update `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc` in the same task** — add or extend:
   - **Anti-pattern** — what failed and why (one line).
   - **Corrected pattern** — copy/paste block that works on this deployment shape.
   - Optional **Lessons learned** bullet under the relevant section (logs, INI paths, service choice).
3. **Do not reuse** the failed command verbatim in future plans — cite the corrected rule text instead.

If the failure reveals a **recurring** gap (not a one-off typo), also add a one-line cross-link in **`deploy-ini-with-code-no-phase-zero.mdc`** or **`hpcperfstats-ini-format.mdc`** when INI/path semantics were wrong.

## What counts as “failed”

- Non-zero exit, `command not found`, wrong container user (`su hpcperfstats` vs root).
- Path does not exist — especially when the command hardcoded `/hpcperfstats/...` instead of INI-resolved paths.
- `docker compose logs pipeline --tail=N` (with or without grep) on long-running pipeline — truncates before stall window; see **No `--tail` on `compose logs`** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`.
- Introspection misuse — unbounded `strace`, `gdb` left attached, or `py-spy` without a target PID when `pgrep`/`ps` should run first (see **Container introspection tools** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Missing `-f docker-compose.app.yaml` (or other overlay) when production uses it.
- Duplicate command blocks that already failed in an earlier plan for the same site.

## Same-task checklist

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1 | Operator paste or error message captured in plan **Completed findings** |
| 2 | Pending block removed or replaced with corrected block |
| 3 | **`compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`** updated (anti-pattern + fix) |
| 4 | New plans use the corrected pattern only |

## Narrow exceptions

- One-off operator typo in the paste (operator ran the wrong block) — fix the plan only; no rule edit required.
- Environment outage (compose down, disk full) — document blocker in plan; no rule change unless the command shape was wrong.

## Overlap

- **`compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`** — authoritative command shape; this rule requires **writing back** failures into that file.
- **`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`** — findings and pending updates on disk only.
- **`deploy-ini-with-code-no-phase-zero.mdc`** — read-only gathering; failures often mean paths should have come from INI first.
- **`hpcperfstats-ini-format.mdc`** — INI key names and sections for path resolution.
